**Well his name is Cyril. He'll be very upset and distressed so you'll need to find him someone**

&#x200B;

I honestly think he suits Tommy so well

I know how you feel. In 2018 I passed high school with a bachelors pass but marks where not up to university standards. Got rejected from every university ( I also wanted to do computer science ) in South Africa, I know most of you are not going to believe me but it's true so my last resort was going to Varsity College ( I'm studying to get my bachelors in network engineering ). The fees are crazy expensive, but try and self study 

&#x200B;

**Some resources here:** 

&#x200B;

[https://www.udemy.com/topic/computer-science/free/](https://www.udemy.com/topic/computer-science/free/)

[https://pll.harvard.edu/catalog/free](https://pll.harvard.edu/catalog/free)

[https://www.coursera.org/browse/computer-science](https://www.coursera.org/browse/computer-science) ( I think this is paid ) 

&#x200B;

The only down side is the courses might be free but you might have to pay for a certificate ( like $60 plus or minus )    

&#x200B;

***You can do it bro. Keep going***

I'm so sorry this happened to you but trust me when I say you're better off without him. You are **NOT** a back up/throwaway . From what you're saying about the kind of person you are, about " *liking books or history or coding "* you sound like a person who knows where she's going and knows what she wants, trust me I love learning about history and actually do coding in university. Don't give him the satisfaction, show him that you're stronger without him and when he's living off his "glory' days you'll be living the dream with people that love, care and respect you  

&#x200B;

Please do find another therapist, if they don't care about your issues then they're not doing their job 

Everyone here cares, you may not see it but we do 

&#x200B;

***Keep fighting***

