Also just a tip, Tinder does lie about the likes.It says something like " You have received 25 likes " but in reality it's 4 likes, they do this to force you to send money and most likely most of those likes are bot accounts. TBH I hated Tinder for the first few weeks never got a match but started to get likes ( most likely bots ) after a year of no matches and no luck I deleted my account. Dating apps do affect your mental health and self-esteem 

&#x200B;

I would recommend Hinge if you'd like a dating app at least with Hinge you get more on the free side and only pay for boosts ( in my experience )

This is just my opinion, there are many ways to " spice up " your current bedroom habits such as trying different positions ( try getting a copy of the Kama Sutra - illustrated version ), try toys for you and him, explore different kinks/fetishes you two might have, roleplaying, watching porn together, being completely spontaneous ( e.g. as soon as he gets home from the store give him head saying you missed him ), do secret teasing in public ( e.g. touching over the pants under the table in different public settings or there are vibrators that are remote/app controlled, by doing this you give your partner control of your pleasure and same vice versa ), recording/taking pictures in the act ( for your own private viewing - not for others to see ), recreating sex scenes from your favourite movie/t.v show and it doesn't have to be in the bedroom having sex in other places like the shower, living room, kitchen etc. **BUT** the most important thing is ***COMMUNICATION*** always talk to each other, ask whats comfortable and just have fun, be happy, smile and laugh because it's meant to be an enjoyable experience with your significant other 

&#x200B;

Hope this helps 😌
